# Copy to `.env` and fill in. `.env` is git-ignored — never commit real keys.
#
# Every TTS provider is optional. Narration only happens when a story sets "voice" (or you pass --voice).
# With no keys at all it still works: Gemini/Deepgram requests fall back to free Edge voices in the
# story's language (Bangla included), and "kokoro" runs fully offline (npm i kokoro-js, English).

# --- Gemini TTS (multilingual — best for Bangla and other non-English narration) ---
#
# One key, or several separated by commas. A key that hits its quota (429 / RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED) rotates
# to the next one; the ring only waits once every key is spent. Duplicates are dropped.
GEMINI_API_KEY=key_one,key_two,key_three
#
# Other accepted spellings (all merged and de-duplicated):
# GEMINI_API_KEYS=key_one,key_two
# GEMINI_API_KEY_1=key_one          (numbered, up to _32)
# GOOGLE_API_KEY=key_four
#
# Any Gemini TTS model works. Give one, or a comma-separated fallback chain (quota is per model, so the next
# model is a fresh pool). `node src/cli.js tts-models` lists what your key can use. Default chain:
# GEMINI_TTS_MODEL=gemini-3.1-flash-tts-preview,gemini-2.5-flash-preview-tts,gemini-2.5-pro-preview-tts

# --- Deepgram Aura-2 (English) ---
# DEEPGRAM_API_KEY=dg_one,dg_two      (same rotation: DEEPGRAM_API_KEYS, DEEPGRAM_API_KEY_1, ...)

# --- Local Kokoro (offline, English) ---
# npm i kokoro-js                     (downloads the ~90 MB model once)
# KOKORO_DTYPE=q8                     (fp32 | fp16 | q8 | q4 | q4f16)

# --- Tuning ---
# VOX_TTS_CONCURRENCY=3               (parallel Gemini/Deepgram requests)
# VOX_TTS_CACHE=output/.tts-cache     (clips are cached by text+voice+model; re-renders cost nothing)
